        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Fundamental Group",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nπ₁(Rⁿ) = 0:\n  Straight-line homotopy: H(t,s) = (1-s)γ(t) + s·x₀ contracts any loop to x₀."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-FUNDAMENTAL-GROUP.md#015",
      "path": [
        "06-FUNDAMENTAL-GROUP.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:06-fundamental-group, git-history:topology:06-fundamental-group]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/06-FUNDAMENTAL-GROUP.md",
        "concepts": "[fundamental, group]",
        "current_path": "topology/06-FUNDAMENTAL-GROUP.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:fundamental-group",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[fundamental, group]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Fundamental Group",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "π₁(Sⁿ) = 0 for n ≥ 2:\n  Any loop misses some point of Sⁿ (by smooth approximation and Sard's theorem).\n  Sⁿ minus a point is homeomorphic to Rⁿ — contractible.\n  So any loop in Sⁿ is contractible. □"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-FUNDAMENTAL-GROUP.md#016",
      "path": [
        "06-FUNDAMENTAL-GROUP.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:topology:06-fundamental-group, git-history:topology:06-fundamental-group]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/06-FUNDAMENTAL-GROUP.md",
        "concepts": "[fundamental, group]",
        "current_path": "topology/06-FUNDAMENTAL-GROUP.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:fundamental-group",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[fundamental, group]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Fundamental Group",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "π₁(convex set) = 0:\n  Straight-line homotopy works for convex subsets of Rⁿ.\n```"
    },
    {
