      },
      "text": "PROOF: The universal cover of S¹ is R (unwrap the circle to the real line).\n  Covering map: p: R → S¹ by p(t) = e^{2πit}.\n  Any loop γ in S¹ based at 1 lifts uniquely to a path γ̃ in R starting at 0.\n  γ̃(1) ∈ Z (since γ̃(0) = 0 and p(γ̃(1)) = p(0) = 1, so γ̃(1) ∈ p^{-1}(1) = Z).\n  The winding number: [γ] ↦ γ̃(1) ∈ Z."
    },
    {
